{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Symptom\n\nThe scheduled `Verify Authorship Identity` workflow fails on every run. Confirmed still\nfailing on the 5 most recent runs through 2026-09-18T18:55Z (head `e12d60a76`).\n\nThe failing job is `verify-identity (authenticated-authorship gate)`; the failing step is\n\"Fail closed if the blobless checkout pack exceeds its limit\". The error is exact:\n\n```\ncheckout pack is 647650 KiB; limit is 563200 KiB\n```\n\nwith `REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB: 563200` in the step environment.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nThis is the authenticated-authorship gate. The pack check is the **second step in the job**,\nahead of `setup-python` and the install, so when it fails the authorship verification never\nexecutes at all. The gate is not failing authorship — it is aborting before reaching it.\n\nWhat is lost is the **periodic whole-store sweep**. Pre-merge authorship verification has NOT\nstopped: `gerrit-verify.yaml` defines its own `verify-identity` job, which performs the same\nwhole-store walk, carries no pack budget, and is what `vote.needs` aggregates into the Verified\nvote — which is why changes have kept earning `Verified +1` throughout this outage. The standalone\n`verify-identity.yml` lane — push, pull_request, workflow_dispatch and the every-6-hours schedule —\nis the sweep that would catch store-wide state a pre-merge walk did not see, and it has produced no\nauthorship verdict since 2026-09-15. A standing red scheduled run also trains readers to ignore the\ngate.\n\n## Root cause (established)\n\nLegitimate growth, not debris. The blobless pack is dominated by the tickets branch history.\nReducing it is the subject of `0894-b9b8-6590-4904`, which tracks restoring the budget to\n100 MiB once the `536b` history reclaim lands. The pack overage is therefore a known,\nseparately-owned condition — not this ticket's defect.\n\nThis ticket's defect is narrower and is the one causing the loss of signal: **a size\nprecondition is ordered ahead of the gate's actual purpose**, so an unrelated budget overage\nsilently disables authorship verification.\n\n## Decision\n\nOperator decision, 2026-09-18: reorder the job so authorship verification runs and reports\nits own verdict first, with the pack check retained, still fail-closed, after it.\n\nExplicitly rejected alternatives:\n\n- Raising the ceiling again — makes the bound track the pack instead of constraining it.\n- Removing or softening the pack check — it is a deliberate safeguard and stays fail-closed.\n- Adding an early-warning monitor for pack growth — does not restore the lost signal.\n- Scoping the pack reduction outside the tickets branch — that is where the growth is, and\n  it is owned by `0894`.\n\nThe job is expected to remain red on the pack step until `0894` lands. That is the correct\noutcome: the budget is genuinely exceeded. What changes is that authorship verification\nexecutes and reports, so the gate produces its signal again.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] Authorship verification executes and reports its own pass/fail verdict on a run whose\n      pack exceeds `REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB`, verified by a run log showing the\n      authorship step's result on such a run.\n- [x] The pack check still runs and still fails the job when the pack exceeds the limit,\n      verified by that same run log showing the job conclusion is failure and the pack step\n      reports the overage.\n- [x] The pack limit value is unchanged at 563200 and the pack step's failure condition is\n      unchanged, verified by the diff.\n- [x] No early-warning or monitoring mechanism is added, verified by the diff.\n- [x] The authorship verdict is legible without expanding a failed step — its outcome is\n      visible in the run's step list, verified by quoting the step conclusions.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789779887509160552,"uuid":"1c8da5d5-eefd-4da2-a46f-fd9dfd8e9311"}